e list can be represented as:</p>

<pre>L<sub>0</sub> =E2=86=92 L<sub>1</sub> =E2=86=92 =E2=80=A6 =E2=86=92 L<=
sub>n - 1</sub> =E2=86=92 L<sub>n</sub>
</pre>

<p><em>Reorder the list to be on the following form:</em></p>

<pre>L<sub>0</sub> =E2=86=92 L<sub>n</sub> =E2=86=92 L<sub>1</sub> =E2=86=
=92 L<sub>n - 1</sub> =E2=86=92 L<sub>2</sub> =E2=86=92 L<sub>n - 2</sub> =
=E2=86=92 =E2=80=A6
</pre>

<p>You may not modify the values in the list's nodes. Only nodes themselves=
 may be changed.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>
<img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/04/reorder=
1linked-list.jpg" style=3D"width: 422px; height: 222px;">
<pre><strong>Input:</strong> head =3D [1,2,3,4]
<strong>Output:</strong> [1,4,2,3]
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>
<img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/09/reorder=
2-linked-list.jpg" style=3D"width: 542px; height: 222px;">
<pre><strong>Input:</strong> head =3D [1,2,3,4,5]
<strong>Output:</strong> [1,5,2,4,3]
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
